WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.149
The Game of Thrones book series is called
A Song of Ice and Fire.

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:10.299
There are five books so far, with more still
being written to finish the story.

00:00:10.299 --> 00:00:15.910
There are also some side books which describe
the history and world of Westeros [and beyond].

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:21.180
And there’s a prequel series called the
Tales of Dunk &amp; Egg – three novellas about

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.949
a knight and his squire set ninety years before
A Game of Thrones.

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:31.569
Compared to the main story, which is huge
and complex and intense, the Tales of Dunk

00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:37.920
&amp; Egg are [relatively] short simple and sweet,
with a lighter tone and smaller scale.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:43.520
But they do have mysteries and secrets of
their own, as well as interesting interconnections

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.230
with the main series.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:50.870
The first story is called The Hedge Knight
– it introduces our heroes Dunk and Egg,

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:55.720
as they’re caught up in events that change
the course of history in Westeros.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.670
The Hedge Knight was adapted to a graphic
novel [comic book] with artwork by Mike S.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.800
Miller and Mike Crowell – which you’ll
see throughout this video.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.659
So what happens in The Hedge Knight, and what
does it mean?

00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:10.950
Our hero is a young man called Dunk.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:17.509
He wasn’t born into a noble family or magic
bloodline like the Starks or Targaryens – he

00:01:17.509 --> 00:01:23.109
was an orphan, in the slums of King’s Landing,
growing up in the alleyways and pot shops

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:24.920
of Flea Bottom [like Davos!].

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:31.319
Dunk isn’t particularly smart or skilled,
but he is extremely tall and strong, and he

00:01:31.319 --> 00:01:35.149
has a good heart – a sense of right and
wrong.

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:39.969
When Dunk was a kid, a knight called Ser Arlan
took Dunk in as his squire.

00:01:39.969 --> 00:01:45.229
Arlan wasn’t a fancy noble knight – he
was a hedge knight, which is more like a mercenary

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:50.079
wandering from place to place, wherever a
lord needs their sword.

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:54.789
Hedge knights have a bad reputation – some
of them become bandits or robbers.

00:01:54.789 --> 00:02:01.270
But Ser Arlan taught Dunk the values of a
true knight – to protect the weak and innocent,

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.009
and to fight for what’s right.

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:08.140
At the start of the story, Ser Arlan dies
– so Dunk feels lost.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.030
He spent his whole life serving Arlan, so
what now?

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.061
[Who should Dunk become?]

00:02:13.061 --> 00:02:17.670
Dunk takes up Arlan’s sword and decides
to be a knight himself.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.090
Thing is, you can’t just decide to be a
knight.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.439
You have to be knighted by another knight
in a special ceremony.

00:02:25.439 --> 00:02:28.900
And it's implied that Dunk was never knighted.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:34.220
He tells people that Arlan knighted him, but
it's hinted that’s a “lie”.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.770
Dunk always gets awkward and evasive when
people ask about his knighting, and he thinks

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.360
to himself that he’s not a knight.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:49.180
But maybe being a true knight is about more
than a ceremony – the story explores what

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.569
it really means to be a hero in a complex
unfair world.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:57.489
Dunk heads for a tournament at Ashford – a
chance to prove himself as a knight.

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:00.170
And along the way, Dunk meets a young boy.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.719
He’s completely bald, and he says his name
is Egg.

00:03:03.719 --> 00:03:09.710
He’s confident and cheeky and asks Dunk
to take him to the tourney as his squire.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:14.060
Dunk refuses at first, so Egg just follows
him until Dunk accepts.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.489
They’ve got sort of a Shrek and Donkey odd
couple dynamic where they annoy each other

00:03:19.489 --> 00:03:23.870
at first, but gradually become unlikely best
friends.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:30.099
The tournament is full of excitement and splendour
– colourful tents and banners, merchants

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:33.430
and entertainers, famous lords and knights..

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:39.769
Warriors from all over Westeros come to joust
and fight – Lannisters, Baratheons and Tyrells,

00:03:39.769 --> 00:03:44.239
Tarlys Freys and Dondarrions – and Targaryens.

00:03:44.239 --> 00:03:49.560
The Hedge Knight is set ninety years ago,
when the Targaryens ruled Westeros.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:54.409
So the king is Daeron Targaryen, and his queen
is Myriah Martell [Daeron made peace with

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:55.409
Dorne by marrying a Dornish princess].

00:03:55.409 --> 00:04:01.200
Daeron's son and heir and Hand of the King
is Prince Baelor Targaryen, called Breakspear.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:07.519
Baelor is a famous knight – he’s chivalrous,
wise, widely loved and respected.

00:04:07.519 --> 00:04:10.739
Baelor comes to the tournament with his son
Valarr.

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:16.450
And Baelor’s brother Prince Maekar comes
with his sons – Daeron Aerion and Aegon.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:21.610
Maekar has another son named Aemon, but he
doesn’t come because he’s studying to

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:27.100
be a maester at the Citadel – Aemon grows
up to become Maester Aemon, Jon’s mentor

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.380
at the Night’s Watch 90 years later.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:36.350
Dunk meets Aerion, and learns he’s a total
asshole [ass sandwich] – he’s rude, cruel,

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:39.780
vain.. think, like, Joffrey with better hair.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:46.550
And Dunk hears that Daeron and Aegon are missing
– apparently they’ve run off somewhere.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:51.290
Dunk wanders the tournament, and gets a crush
on a girl called Tanselle who works a puppet

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.290
show.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:57.720
He hires her to paint a sigil on his shield,
to represent himself as a knight – he chooses

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:03.380
an elm tree with a shooting star – cause
Dunk saw a shooting star at camp the other

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.380
night.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:09.530
And instead of calling himself Ser Dunk, he
invents the name “Ser Duncan the Tall”.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.620
So Dunk creates an identity for himself as
a knight.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.150
But what kind of knight is he?

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:21.470
Is he cruel and vain like Aerion, or chivalrous
like Baelor Breakspear?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:25.009
What does it really mean to be a hero?

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:29.210
That night, Prince Aerion attacks the puppet
girl Tanselle.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:34.430
Cause Tanselle performed a puppet show about
a dragon being slain – and Aerion considers

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:41.539
himself a Targaryen dragon, so he gets offended
and starts breaking Tanselle's fingers.

00:05:41.539 --> 00:05:48.090
So Dunk instinctively runs in and beats up
Aerion, to defend this damsel in distress.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.729
It’s the right thing to do – but it’s
also a foolish thing to do.

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:57.710
Westeros is unfair, and hedge knights are
not allowed to hit royal princes [even if

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.389
that prince is a cunt] – Dunk could be punished
with death [and Tanselle still won’t be

00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:01.389
spared].

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:04.129
So is this heroism or stupidity?

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:09.240
In Tanselle’s puppet show, she says “All
men are fools, and all men are knights”.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:16.219
It means we all have some desire to be a romantic
hero – to save maidens and fight dragons

00:06:16.219 --> 00:06:23.500
– and that feeling is ridiculous and foolish
but it’s also part of what makes us human.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:29.290
Aerion almost has Dunk killed on the spot,
but he’s saved by Egg.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:35.250
It turns out that Egg is not some random peasant
– he’s actually Prince Aegon Targaryen,

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:40.000
son of Prince Maekar, and grandson of the
king.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.610
Egg explains that his father Maekar wanted
Daeron to ride in the tournament, with Egg

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.110
as his squire.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:52.479
But Daeron hates riding and fighting, so instead
he ran off and got drunk – and he shaved

00:06:52.479 --> 00:06:59.919
Egg’s head to hide his silvery-gold blond
hair, which is famously a feature of Targaryens.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:03.870
Egg says Daeron didn’t need to shave, cause
he just has brown hair.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:09.260
He mentions that their uncle Baelor also has
dark hair instead of blonde, because of his

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.919
Dornish mother.

00:07:10.919 --> 00:07:15.800
All this talk about Targaryen hair colour
might be a hint supporting the theory that

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:20.260
Jon Snow is the son of Rhaegar Targaryen and
Lyanna Stark.

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:25.919
The story is showing us that not all Targaryens
are blonde – so Jon Snow could be Rhaegar

00:07:25.919 --> 00:07:31.330
Targaryen’s son, but have the dark hair
of his mother Lyanna.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:36.009
So anyway Daeron went on a bender, but Egg
still wanted to be a squire at the tournament,

00:07:36.009 --> 00:07:38.720
so that’s why he attached himself to Dunk.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:44.770
Egg apologises for lying about his identity,
but Dunk forgives him, because he also lied

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:50.340
to get what he wanted – implying that Dunk
lied to become a knight, just like Egg lied

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:52.450
to become a squire.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.960
Egg points out that he and Dunk are both from
King’s Landing – even though Dunk is from

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.729
the slums of Flea Bottom, while Prince Aegon
is from the palace on the hill.

00:08:01.729 --> 00:08:05.930
So the story often explores Dunk and Egg’s
different perspectives from their different

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.100
social classes.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:11.020
Aerion demands that Dunk be punished.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:18.120
So Dunk asks for a trial by combat, and Aerion
raises the stakes, demanding a trial of seven.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:22.409
A trial of seven is fight of seven men against
seven.

00:08:22.409 --> 00:08:27.389
So Dunk and Aerion each need to find six allies,
to fight alongside them.

00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:32.909
This is pretty unfair for Dunk, because Prince
Aerion can easily get his Kingsguard knights,

00:08:32.909 --> 00:08:35.500
and his father and brother to fight with him.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:40.219
It’s much harder for Dunk to find allies,
cause no one knows who he is – and who would

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:45.610
want to risk their life to fight for a hedge
knight against Targaryen princes?

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:48.950
But Dunk and Egg find some allies.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:53.760
Egg knows one guy, and a couple more want
revenge on Aerion for being such a prick [in

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:54.760
the jousting].

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:58.300
And this [absolute chad] bloke Lyonel Baratheon
signs up purely for the fuggen banter [clout]

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:02.610
– this is the first trial of seven in a
hundred years, and Lyonel doesn’t wanna

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.610
miss out.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:08.430
Lyonel is a famous knight – he’s called
“The Laughing Storm” for his habit of

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.959
laughing at his opponents while he beats them
up.

00:09:11.959 --> 00:09:16.829
Lyonel is an ancestor of King Bobby B and
Gendry and Stannis and Shireen.

00:09:16.829 --> 00:09:22.820
And we know from the history book that years
later, Lyonel fights against Dunk – but

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:25.010
that’s another story.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.290
Dunk also recruits young Raymun Fossoway.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.839
Raymun has a falling out with his cousin Steffon.

00:09:30.839 --> 00:09:36.480
Cause Steffon betrays Dunk by promising to
fight for him, then joining Aerion instead

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:40.160
– cause Aerion promises to make him a lord.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.320
This creates a split in House Fossoway that
still remains to this day – Steffon’s

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:50.120
line are the red-apple Fossoways, while Raymun’s
are the green-apple Fossoways – cause Raymun

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:56.670
would rather be an unripe green apple than
a rotten wormy red one like Steffon.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:10:01.620
So on the morning of the trial, Aerion has
seven knights, but Dunk desperately needs

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.940
one more.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:08.410
He begs the crowd for a volunteer, asks “ARE
THERE NO TRUE KNIGHTS AMONG YOU?”.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:12.180
Cause every knight swears an oath to defend
the innocent.

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:15.850
But all these knights and high lords refuse
him.

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:21.389
Cause the nobility like Steffon Fossoway have
selfish political reasons to side with their

00:10:21.389 --> 00:10:23.899
prince even when their prince is wrong.

00:10:23.899 --> 00:10:29.060
It’s only a poor lowborn man like Dunk,
who has no political prospects, and nothing

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:34.990
to lose, who’s willing to fight for what’s
right – which shows the corruption and injustice

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.230
of this feudal class system.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:42.339
But just when all hope seems lost, Prince
Baelor Breakspear joins Dunk [to fight against

00:10:42.339 --> 00:10:45.660
his brother Maekar and his nephews], and says
Dunk was a “true knight” to fight against

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.940
Aerion.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:50.350
So maybe there is hope for justice.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:56.070
The combat begins, and fourteen armoured knights
crash together.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:11:00.280
Dunk gets knocked off his horse, and Aerion
gets the upper hand.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:04.250
Dunk is not as skilled or trained as Prince
Aerion.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:07.160
But once they’re down in the mud, Dunk has
the advantage.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.899
Cause Dunk has experience fighting dirty on
the rough streets of Flea Bottom, so he’s

00:11:11.899 --> 00:11:15.670
able to defeat Aerion and end the trial.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:21.310
So for a moment it seems that this Game of
Thrones story has a happy ending – Dunk

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.920
the heroic underdog gets justice over the
prince.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:31.950
But-- Prince Baelor is acting weird, all confused
and slurry.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:37.810
When they pull off his helmet, some of his
brain falls out – his head got smashed in

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:38.850
in the fight.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:44.520
So Prince Baelor Breakspear falls to the ground
and dies.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.779
Everyone is horrified by Baelor’s death.

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:52.760
He was heir to the throne, loved by all, everyone
thought he would be a great king.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:58.279
So at the funeral, Baelor’s son Valarr asks
why the gods would take Prince Baelor for

00:11:58.279 --> 00:12:00.949
the sake of Dunk the hedge knight?

00:12:00.949 --> 00:12:03.769
What kind of justice is this?

00:12:03.769 --> 00:12:06.060
Dunk speaks with Baelor’s brother Maekar.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:11.050
Maekar was always resentful living in the
shadow of his more popular brother – kind

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.949
of like how Stannis is resentful of Robert.

00:12:13.949 --> 00:12:20.070
But Maekar reveals that that it was his mace
that killed Baelor – it was an accident,

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:24.370
but now he has to live with the knowledge
that he killed his big brother.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.449
[like how Stannis feels guilt that he killed
his brother Renly].

00:12:25.449 --> 00:12:30.550
So like Valarr, Maekar asks ‘what’s the
meaning of this tragedy?’

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:37.300
Dunk says that maybe Baelor dying to save
Dunk will have meaning if, one day, the realm

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:38.600
needs Dunk.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:41.740
Maybe Dunk has a special destiny.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:45.920
Baelor’s death is actually the fulfilment
of a prophecy.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:52.040
Cause before the trial, Daeron comes to Dunk
and apologises for siding with Aerion.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:57.200
Daeron feels like he’s a failure and a disappointment
to his [hardarse] [demanding] father Maekar,

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:03.630
and uses drinking and sex to cope – similar
to Tyrion’s relationship with his father.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.830
But Daeron also says that he had a dream about
Dunk.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:13.450
In the dream, there was a dragon, and the
dragon dies, but Dunk survives.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:18.170
Daeron hopes that the dead dragon means that
that Aerion will die – but as it turns out,

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:21.149
the dragon who dies is Baelor.

00:13:21.149 --> 00:13:25.690
This fits the pattern of many prophecies and
dreams in the series – they come true, but

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:27.959
in an unexpected way.

00:13:27.959 --> 00:13:33.839
Many Targaryens have prophetic dreams that
lead to destruction.

00:13:33.839 --> 00:13:38.269
We know from the history book that after The
Hedge Knight, King Daeron and Prince Valarr

00:13:38.269 --> 00:13:40.120
die in a plague.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:43.430
When King Daeron’s other sons die, Maekar
becomes king.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:48.600
But then Maekar dies in battle, Daeron the
Drunken dies of the clap, and Aerion drinks

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:53.320
wildfire cause he thinks it’ll transform
him into a dragon, which leaves the realm

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:56.170
in a big ol succession pickle.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.829
Who should be the next king?

00:13:58.829 --> 00:14:03.240
Daeron and Aerion both had kids, but no one
wants them on the Throne.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.759
So they offer Maester Aemon the throne, but
he refuses.

00:14:06.759 --> 00:14:12.980
So the next King of Westeros is Egg – he
becomes King Aegon Targaryen the Fifth.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:18.250
And King Egg chooses Dunk to lead his Kingsguard
– so Dunk from Flea Bottom rises to the

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:22.019
highest position for a knight in Westeros.

00:14:22.019 --> 00:14:27.759
King Egg’s rule was difficult, with rebellious
lords and rebellious children.

00:14:27.759 --> 00:14:32.639
And later in life, he became convinced that
the solution to all his problems was dragons

00:14:32.639 --> 00:14:37.870
– he was obsessed with tryina hatch some
dragon eggs – experimenting with sorcery,

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:40.389
wildfire, and ancient lore.

00:14:40.389 --> 00:14:46.649
And this dream of dragons ended in tragedy
– a mysterious fire at Summerhall killed

00:14:46.649 --> 00:14:50.959
King Egg and most of his family and Dunk.

00:14:50.959 --> 00:14:55.800
One of the only survivors was Egg’s granddaughter
Rhaella – and it’s hinted that she was

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.940
saved from the fire by Dunk before he died.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:06.010
Then while Summerhall burned behind her, Rhaella
gave birth to Rhaegar Targaryen – the brother

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:10.540
of Viserys and Daenerys, and the father of
Jon Snow.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:15.529
So maybe Dunk was right – there was a day
when the realm needed him.

00:15:15.529 --> 00:15:20.490
If it wasn’t for Dunk saving Rhaella, Rhaegar
and Daenerys and Jon Snow would never have

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:23.360
been born, the whole series wouldn’t have
happened.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.890
And all of this began with Dunk seeing the
comet that inspired his heraldry.

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:33.580
A comet, or bleeding star, is part of the
prophecy of Azor Ahai, the hero that’ll

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:38.769
save the world – Rhaegar believed that his
son would be this hero, when he saw a falling

00:15:38.769 --> 00:15:39.769
star.

00:15:39.769 --> 00:15:44.430
So Dunk is deeply connected to the prophetic
destiny of Westeros.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:50.329
But will this destiny save Westeros, or lead
to more fire and tragedy?

00:15:50.329 --> 00:15:54.380
Dunk says we never know what the morrow will
bring.

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:59.279
All he can do is try his best to be a true
knight.

00:15:59.279 --> 00:16:03.370
The Hedge Knight asks ‘what does it mean
to be true knight?’

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:08.980
It’s clearly not about being a highborn
noble warrior with sword and armour – cause

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.949
Aerion’s a low quality individual.

00:16:10.949 --> 00:16:16.910
And it’s not about being skilled or smart,
cause Dunk isn’t – it was Dunk’s foolish

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:20.380
romantic impulse that led him to be a hero
in the first place.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:25.910
It’s not about a special ceremony, and it’s
not about telling the truth – Dunk and Egg

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:28.380
both lie to get to the tourney.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:33.279
A big part of what makes Dunk a hero is his
humility.

00:16:33.279 --> 00:16:37.240
Noble lords and knights have too much to lose
to wanna fight for justice.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:43.079
But Dunk has nothing to lose but his honour,
and that’s why he risks everything to protect

00:16:43.079 --> 00:16:44.209
others.

00:16:44.209 --> 00:16:48.370
As a lowborn commoner, he’s more sympathetic
to other common people.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:54.019
And Dunk’s humble origins allow him to beat
Aerion – using dirty Flea Bottom fighting

00:16:54.019 --> 00:16:57.130
tricks to beat the fancy prince.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:17:00.160
Humility helps make Dunk a true knight.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:05.710
So at the end of story, Maekar offers for
Dunk and Egg to join his knights at his castle.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:11.090
But instead, Dunk takes Egg on the road, to
live as a hedge knight – cause that humility

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:16.170
will help Egg grow into a better man, and
a better king.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:23.670
The story criticises a corrupt system of nobility,
and celebrates a more humble ideal of heroism,

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:28.910
where anyone with courage and strength and
compassion can be a true knight [being a seven

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:29.910
foot tall bloke helps too].

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:33.840
90 years later, Brienne’s story explores
the same themes.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:39.360
Like Dunk, she’s technically not a knight,
she’s not particularly smart or special.

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:45.290
But she’s strong and brave and selfless
and determined to what’s right, which makes

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:49.430
her more of a true knight than almost any
actual knight.

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:55.020
In Book 4, Brienne describes an old shield
from her father’s armoury which looks exactly

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:58.350
like Dunk’s shield with the tree and star.

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:03.980
So for years, fans have speculated that Brienne
and Dunk are related, and at a convention,

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:10.160
author George Martin confirmed that Dunk is
Brienne’s ancestor – possibly her great-grandpa.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:16.510
So Dunk’s legacy as a humble true knight
continues in Brienne.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:21.190
At the end of The Hedge Knight, Dunk &amp; Egg
head off for more adventures – there are

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.950
two more Dunk &amp; Egg stories after The Hedge
Knight.

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:28.160
And you can get all of them on audiobook for
